citation_anchor_rot_check --resolve-targets  (criteria 2026-10-14.1)
  PREDICATE, printed with the result rather than described: the citations are whatever extract() finds -- LINECITE_RE = (?:[A-Za-z0-9_./\\-]+\.(?:html|js|cjs|mjs|py|sql|md|json|tla|cfg)):\d+ -- and a citation RESOLVES when its file exists in this clone and has at least that many lines.
  198 qualified `file.ext:NNN` citation(s), 323 bare `:NNNN`, 521 total -- the same extractor the headline count uses

  RESOLVES     198  the file exists and is at least that long
  PAST-EOF       0  DEFINITELY stale -- no reading of the document makes these right
  FILE-ABSENT    0  the cited file is not in this clone
  UNRESOLVABLE 323  bare `:NNNN` -- target is whatever the prose says. NOT counted as fresh and NOT as stale.

  AT-RISK, measured from git rather than from reading either side: blame the document line for when the citation was AUTHORED (author time, not commit time -- a rebase rewrites the latter), then count commits touching the cited file since.
  AT-RISK      160  the cited file moved after the citation was written. A POPULATION TO RE-CHECK, not a defect count.
  SETTLED       38  nothing has touched the cited file since
  UNKNOWN        0  blame or log could not answer -- kept out of both counts
